    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0321" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v32/pg286"/>

                <head>115. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in the Dominican Republic<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d115-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1965-07-31T13:11:00-04:00">July 31, 1965, 1:11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p>164. For Bunker and Bennett. We have been closely following
                    negotiations and development of political situation in Dominican Republic. We
                    have also been continually assessing attitude of public and government officials
                    and other American Republics as well as public opinion in the United States. It
                    is becoming more apparent than ever that we must move quickly to a definitive
                    solution in the Dominican Republic before the situation deteriorates beyond
                    repair.</p>
                <p>Our assessment overall situation (Dominican Republic, hemisphere, world) is that
                    it is reaching boiling point much the same as you encountered in Dominican
                    Republic in middle of June when OAS Committee
                    felt compelled make its proposal on June 18 before you had opportunity fully
                    review it in Washington.</p>
                <p>When you departed Washington after reporting MFM<anchor n="2" xml:id="d115-f2"/> you thought solution could be
                    obtained in approximately two weeks. Request your current assessment.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d115-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Rusk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d115-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d115-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives and Records Administration, RG 59, Central Files
                    1964–66, POL 15 DOM REP. Secret; Immediate; Exdis. Drafted and approved by Sayre on July 31.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d115-f2" n="2" xml:id="d115-f2-content">
                <p>
                    Bunker departed the Dominican Republic for
                    Washington the morning of July 16 for consultations at the White House and to
                    report to the OAS. No record of Bunkerʼs meeting at the White House has been
                    found. Bunker returned to the Dominican
                    Republic on Monday, July 19.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d115-f3" n="3" xml:id="d115-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d117">Document 117</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
